<Base title="How we measure | Paperboat status" description="How Paperboat's status page decides what to show.">
  <section class="card how">
    <h1 class="card-title">How we measure</h1>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Checks:</b> real actions, every minute, from independent locations.</li>
      <li><b>Down:</b> two locations each fail three checks in a row. <b>Degraded:</b> some parts fail or are slow.</li>
      <li><b>Back to normal:</b> five passes in a row. No data for 3 minutes shows "Status data delayed", never green.</li>
      <li><b>Uptime:</b> a major-outage minute counts as down, a degraded minute as 30% down; minutes without data are left out.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <div class="center"><a class="btn btn-quiet" href="/">Back to status</a></div>
</Base>
